    "text": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented a bounded stack in Cuis Smalltalk with comprehensive tests. Here's what was created:\n\n## BoundedStack Class\nLocated in category `BoundedStack`, with:\n- **Instance variables**: `items` (Array), `top` (current index), `capacity`\n- **Methods**:\n  - `new:` (class method) - creates stack with positive integer capacity\n  - `initialize:` - sets up empty stack\n  - `push:` - adds object to top\n  - `pop` - removes and returns top element\n  - `top` - returns top element without removing\n  - `isEmpty` - true if no elements\n  - `size` - returns current element count\n\n## Test Suite\n16 comprehensive tests in category `BoundedStack-Tests` covering:\n- \u2705 Valid stack creation with various capacities\n- \u2705 Error validation: non-positive and non-integer capacities\n- \u2705 Error messages for invalid operations\n- \u2705 Push/pop operations and LIFO behavior\n- \u2705 `top` operation (non-destructive access)\n- \u2705 Full stack behavior (push on full fails)\n- \u2705 Empty stack behavior (pop/top on empty fail)\n- \u2705 Alternating push/pop patterns\n- \u2705 Edge case of capacity 1\n- \u2705 Different object types (integers, strings, symbols, arrays, nil)\n\nAll tests pass and the image has been saved."
